        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[PAGI: What happens to a Send in Flight? ]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[John the contract of connection management in PAGI. The article explains how both send and receive futures can be resolved without exceptions when the client has disconnected thus avoiding the complexity of manual exception handling and allowing for predictable and consistent transition states.]]></description>
            <pubDate>2026.08.29</pubDate>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://dev.to/jjn1056/wpens-to-a-send-in-flightpolishing-pagis-disconnect-contract-1n34</guid>
            <link>https://dev.to/jjn1056/wpens-to-a-send-in-flightpolishing-pagis-disconnect-contract-1n34</link>
            
            
            
            <author><![CDATA[john_napiorkowski]]></author>
            
                
            
            
        </item>
        
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[PAGI::Server 0.002007: One Contract, Two Transports]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[A full explanation of the conformance pass has been provided by John Napiorkowski, aimed at making transport protocols invisible to applications. The release bounds the scope of event validation to an unconditional validation of events at all outgoing paths, harmonises flow-control mechanisms, and defines a uniform token for indicating the reason for disconnection to provide complete reliability for error messages.]]></description>
            <pubDate>2026.08.24</pubDate>
            <guid isPermaLink="false">https://dev.to/jjn1056/pagiserver-0002007-one-contract-two-transports-4mce</guid>
            <link>https://dev.to/jjn1056/pagiserver-0002007-one-contract-two-transports-4mce</link>
            
            
            
            <author><![CDATA[john_napiorkowski]]></author>
            
                
            
            
        </item>
        
        <item>
            <title><![CDATA[Template::Stencil - A Fast Template Engine]]></title>
            <description><![CDATA[Using Template::Stencil, a template is parsed once into packed bytecode in a single memory arena, and rendered by a threaded C interpreter that writes straight into an SV-backed buffer. I don't think any other template engine does this.]]></description>
            <pubDate>2026.08.30</pubDate>
